  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n The Hidden Cost of Higher Valuations\nHi Sara,\nPrivate equity is flooding into the accounting firm space. Valuations are rising. Buyers are circling. On the surface, it looks like a seller\u2019s dream.\nBut here\u2019s what no one\u2019s talking about:\nHigher valuations are quietly killing the traditional family succession plan.\nLast year alone, I saw five owners pass over their own children - children who had been working in the business for years - because third-party buyers could offer more.\nWhy? Because:\nValuations have jumped\n\nInterest rates make internal buyouts unaffordable\n\nSBA loans are normalizing 90% cash at close-hard to compete with that\n\nWhen you can sell for several million dollars tomorrow, most sellers aren\u2019t going to accept a 10-year buyout from their child at a fraction of the price. And most parents don\u2019t want their kid saddled with that kind of debt.\u00a0\nIt\u2019s not a moral failing. It\u2019s math.\nThat math has real consequences, especially for buyers stepping into family-run firms. If the seller\u2019s child is still working in the business, you\u2019re walking into a complex emotional and legal situation.\nAnd without a solid employment agreement, that person could leave and take clients with them.\nThis shift isn\u2019t just about who\u2019s buying. It\u2019s about how succession works now.\nCurious how to navigate succession when emotions (and millions of dollars) are on the line?\nWatch the full breakdown here.\nBecause making a smart exit shouldn't mean torching the family tree.\nTo smarter deals (and smoother exits),\nSara Sharp\nDeal Attorney & Founder of Deal Academy\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
